      ime: "Washington",
      vrsta: "grad",
      sazetak: "The capital, where the most important museums and monuments are free and the history of the USA can be read in stone.",
      prica: [
        "The city was founded in 1790 specifically to serve as the capital, on land along the Potomac River chosen by George Washington. The French engineer Pierre L'Enfant envisioned it with broad diagonal avenues and a long green axis that today is called the National Mall.",
        "The British burned the Capitol and the White House in 1814, but the city was rebuilt and over time gained the monuments and museums that make it one great open-air classroom. The Height of Buildings Act of 1910 is the reason there are no skyscrapers here."
      ],
      vidjeti: [
        { ime: "Lincoln Memorial", opis: "The 1922 temple has 36 columns, one for each state at the time of Lincoln's death. On the steps, look for the engraved spot from which Martin Luther King delivered his “I Have a Dream” speech in 1963." },
        { ime: "Washington Monument", opis: "The 169-meter obelisk was completed in 1884, after construction had been halted for more than twenty years by a lack of money and the Civil War. About a third of the way up you can clearly see a change in the color of the marble, at the point where work resumed." },
        { ime: "The Capitol", opis: "The seat of Congress is crowned by a cast-iron dome that was completed in the middle of the Civil War, because Lincoln wanted to show that the Union would endure. At the top stands the bronze Statue of Freedom, facing east." },
        { ime: "Smithsonian museums", opis: "The institution was founded in 1846 with money from James Smithson, a British scientist who never set foot in the USA, and admission to all its museums is free. The National Museum of African American History and Culture, opened in 2016, stands out in particular, and you walk through it from the bottom up, from slavery to the present day." },
        { ime: "Vietnam Veterans Memorial", opis: "The black granite wall was designed by Maya Lin while she was still a 21-year-old student. The names of the fallen are arranged by date of casualty, and in the polished stone visitors see their own reflection." },
        { ime: "Library of Congress", opis: "The Thomas Jefferson Building of 1897 has a lavishly painted Great Hall and a circular reading room that you can view from the gallery. The exhibits include a Gutenberg Bible, one of the rare complete copies on vellum." }
      ],
      jesti: [
        { ime: "Half-smoke", opis: "A coarse, half-smoked sausage in a bun, topped with chili, onions and mustard. It is the city's signature bite, traditionally eaten in the diners on U Street." },
        { ime: "Crab cakes", opis: "Patties of blue crab meat from the nearby Chesapeake Bay, seasoned with Old Bay spice mix." },
        { ime: "Ethiopian cuisine", opis: "Washington has one of the largest Ethiopian communities outside Africa, so this is a wonderful place to eat stews served on injera, a soft, slightly sour flatbread that also serves as your utensil." }
      ],
      dozivjeti: [
        { ime: "The National Mall at dusk", opis: "If you want to experience the monuments without the crowds and the heat, walk from the Lincoln Memorial to the World War II Memorial after sunset, when they are all lit up. Park rangers give free talks.", link: "https://www.nps.gov/nama/index.htm" },
        { ime: "U Street and the music of the city", opis: "This street was once called Black Broadway, and Duke Ellington was born nearby in 1899. Today the clubs play jazz and go-go, a homegrown funk rhythm that was named the city's official music in 2020." },
        { ime: "Arlington National Cemetery", opis: "Across the river you can watch the changing of the guard at the Tomb of the Unknown Soldier, which is carried out in complete silence, and see the eternal flame at the grave of John F. Kennedy.", link: "https://www.arlingtoncemetery.mil/" },
        { ime: "The Library of Congress reading room", opis: "If you love books and architecture, reserve a free timed pass to tour the Thomas Jefferson Building.", link: "https://www.loc.gov/visit/" }
      ],
      agencije: [
        { ime: "Destination DC", opis: "The city's official tourism organization.", link: "https://washington.org/" },
        { ime: "National Park Service: National Mall", opis: "Official information on the monuments, ranger-led programs and tickets for the Washington Monument.", link: "https://www.nps.gov/nama/index.htm" }
      ],
      kada: "The loveliest time is late March and early April, when the cherry trees that Tokyo gave the city in 1912 are in bloom. Reserve free timed tickets for the most popular museums and monuments in advance."
